GetDP 3.5.0 (tag getdp_3_5_0, 864875cd) -- patch set "mpx3"

Supersedes "mpx2", which it contains unchanged (and through it "mpx1",
getdp-3.5.0-mpx1-mpi-nonlocal-prealloc.patch). Four independent changes plus
the version suffix; changes 3 and 4 are new in mpx3:

1. MPI: per-row preallocation of the locally owned matrix rows (= mpx1).
   [src/kernel/LinAlg_PETSC.cpp]
   Unpatched GetDP 3.5.0 creates the distributed (MPIAIJ) matrix with a
   uniform -petsc_prealloc guess (default 100) per row for both the diagonal
   and the off-diagonal blocks, ignoring the "non-local equations" (dense rows
   produced by global quantities / Integral-type couplings such as a Floquet
   DtN map). Under MPI each dense row then triggers repeated reallocations of
   the local matrix during assembly. This passes per-row d_nnz/o_nnz to
   MatCreateAIJ, mirroring the sequential nnz[] vector (non-local rows get
   full lines, capped by the existing 500 MB -petsc_prealloc_full heuristic
   and by the block widths). Local sizes come from PetscSplitOwnership, i.e.
   identical to PETSC_DECIDE: same layout, same results. Sequential runs are
   not affected.

2. No fixed limit on the number of groups of entities per element.
   [src/interface/ProData.h, src/kernel/Get_DofOfElement.cpp,
    src/kernel/Get_ElementSource.cpp]
   struct Element held NumGroupsOfEntities, NbrEntitiesInGroups,
   NumEntitiesInGroups[..][NBR_MAX_ENTITIES_IN_ELEMENT], NumSubFunction[3][..]
   and GlobalBasisFunction[..] as fixed arrays of NBR_MAX_GROUPS_IN_ELEMENT
   (200; 30 with HAVE_SMALL_STACK) entries, with "Reached limit number of
   groups of entities" past 198 (the FIXME in ProData.h). Each global
   (BF_Region / BF_Global) basis function adds one group on every element of
   its support, so e.g. a Floquet DtN with two global unknowns per order and
   side failed above ~99 orders. The arrays are now std::vector members
   (NumEntitiesInGroups: vector of std::array rows), grown geometrically by a
   single helper (Grow_GroupsOfEntities) before each insertion and never
   shrunk: after warm-up the per-element hot paths do not allocate, and
   elements that never use groups (post-processing, cuts) allocate nothing.
   All index-based accesses are unchanged; the three call sites passing the
   arrays as int* use .data(). The ElementTrace candidates, previously
   Malloc'ed (raw memory), are now created with new / delete since struct
   Element has non-trivial members. NBR_MAX_GROUPS_IN_ELEMENT is removed
   (no other use). Below the old limit the behaviour is unchanged
   (validated byte-identical outputs vs mpx1). sizeof(struct Element) drops
   from 57936 to 4504 bytes (x86-64; much less stack per local Element).

3. Tabulated Gauss rules on quadrangles: wrong ordinates corrected.
   [src/kernel/Gauss_Quadrangle.h]
   3 points: yq3 held +-0.840896415255 where the degree-2 rule needs
   +-1/sqrt(2) = +-0.7071067811865476. 7 points: the last four entries of
   yq7 held +-sqrt(3/5) = +-0.7745966692414834 where the degree-5 rule
   needs +-1/sqrt(3) = +-0.5773502691896258. With the values of GetDP 3.5.0
   both rules integrate exactly only polynomials of degree 1 in v (the
   integral of v^2 over the reference square comes out as 1.8856 and 1.9259
   instead of 4/3), without any message. Abscissae and weights are unchanged.
   The other tabulated rules (lines, triangles, tetrahedra, hexahedra) are
   unchanged.

4. Integral post-quantities accept the GaussLegendre integration type.
   [src/kernel/Cal_PostQuantity.cpp]
   Cal_PostQuantity refused every integration case whose type is not Gauss
   ("Only numerical integration is available in Integral PostQuantities"),
   although the code that follows reads the points through the same
   Quadrature function as the assembly, which accepts both types. The test
   now accepts GaussLegendre as well.

5. CMakeLists.txt: GETDP_EXTRA_VERSION "-mpx3" (`getdp --version` prints
   3.5.0-mpx3-git-864875cd when built from the git tag, 3.5.0-mpx3 from the
   release tarball).

Apply with:  cd getdp && git apply <this file>   (or: patch -p1 < <this file>)

